      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso",
          "value": "<p>in hardship. Although our forefathers in the generations of our teachers faced greater adversity than ourselves\u2014for example, in the time of R. Judah ben R. Ilai, when six students would cover themselves in one garment and study Torah [see b. Sanhedrin 20a], and Hillel the elder, and similar examples\u2014we have declined from those generations.</p>\n<p>Now, light of my eyes, our God has given you as a towering citadel to the scholars, a fortress to the academy heads, a refuge to the students, and a helping hand for those in need, a source of bread and water for a multitude of God\u2019s people. Look with love upon the covenant that existed between my forefathers, the geonim, and your dear forefathers, and the fraternity and friendship between them, and follow the custom of your fathers with my fathers and remember me with a generous donation in my name. Do not neglect to acknowledge me as I desire.</p>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
